  "limits": "The animation stores keyframes as morph targets, so vertices move along chords between keyframes: the largest deviation from the true rotation is 1 - cos(step/2) of the radius (0.0086 for the example with 48 frames and rate 2). Tubes are unlit three-sided prisms whose positions are morphed without normal targets. The logarithm is ill-conditioned for nearly isoclinic rotations, where the invariant planes are not unique, and picks one plane pair for rotations by pi.",
